{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he shall take for the one being purified.</b> The priest shall take from his own. And some say the one with tzara'at shall give them. The tav of the hitpa'el is absorbed in the dagesh of the tet, and it is on the pattern of איש מתהלל." "<b>Two birds.</b> Every bird is called צפור, and so he may take any bird he finds:" "<b>Alive.</b> And not dead:" "<b>Pure.</b> That he not take from the impure ones:" "<b>And cedar wood and hyssop.</b> It is the greatest and smallest among the species of plants, and the proof is from the words of Solomon's wisdom. And there is no need to search concerning the hyssop, for it is known by tradition. And so the one with tzara'at and the afflicted house and corpse impurity are related, and they too are like the model of the Passover of Egypt:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "The comment refers to the vocalization and morphological pattern of למטהר, explaining the assimilation of the hitpa'el tav into the following consonant."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:02.941893648Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}